A||||8||Oreif||Check out my new battery. (see pic)||||14||
Z||000000||Oreif||12-20-2001||02:43 PM||||Hey All,<BR> I bought an Optima Gel-Cell Battery off of Ebay. These were a close-out special so there was no label on the top. (Case is stamped Optima and the original box was an Optima) Anyhow, The top was blank so I "borrowed" an image from Haze's website, using photoshop, a laser printer, a laminating machine, and some clear topcoat (to seal the edges from water).<BR>Here is what it looks like:<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/new_bat.jpg">  <P>BTW ~ For those with an eye for detail, The decklid is off having the IMSA spoiler installed. The battery isn't connected since the car is "resting" thru the winter.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">            <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 12-20-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000001||The Fieromaster||12-20-2001||03:06 PM||||Just to warn you... There are vent holes on batteries...  Battery vapors explosive... Just make sure you didnt cover vent holes!  Although i dunno about THAT battery... my buddy has some kind of round cell battery and it had no vents and it was made to beable to mount in any position!?!<P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">        <FONT COLOR="red"><B>"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT></B>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/thefieromastersig.gif">    <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AOL IM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="green">1992 Mitsubishi Eclipse GS ~ soon will be turboed</FONT><BR></B>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex4mula||12-20-2001||03:06 PM||||Looks very nice  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">. Do Optimas come in yellow too? If so I may get one for my soon to be yellow Formula.<P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red-Original Owner & White-1/94 with PM (:||||reg||14
Z||000003||MinnGreenGT||12-20-2001||03:07 PM||||Looks cool!  And yes, the Optima is the sealed battery that can be mounted anywhere at any angle.<P>Oreif- does the seller have any more?<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||The Fieromaster||12-20-2001||03:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B>Looks cool!  And yes, the Optima is the sealed battery that can be mounted anywhere at any angle.<P>Oreif- does the seller have any more?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Really? cool! Just didnt want him to blow up his car ya know... Hmm i wonder how think it is?  Could tuck her away smaller in the front compartement if she is nice and thin and you lay her on her side.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||12-20-2001||05:41 PM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B>Looks cool!  And yes, the Optima is the sealed battery that can be mounted anywhere at any angle.<P>Oreif- does the seller have any more?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes he has more. He does dutch auctions on them. Right now he has 14 of them. The price is $69.95. I called around by me and the least expensive was $109.95 + tax. I won it at $69.95 and it was $21.95 for shipping.<BR> <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=1311978947" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=1311978947</A> <P>NOTE: in the ad it shows label on the battery, Mine had no labels on it and it was in the original box wrapped in plastic and foam.<P>Optima batteries come in different colors for different uses. <BR>Red = Automotive<BR>Yellow = Deep Cycle<BR>Blue = Marine use (Boats)<P>They do have vents on them but they are actually more like pressure relief ports. They are in the back. There are no vents on top, it was a very smooth surface. Since it's a Gel-Cell it does not matter which way you mount it. As you can see it also has both types of hook-ups top and sidemount.<BR>It's 900 Cold Cranking Amps<BR>At 0*F it has 700 Cold Cranking Amps.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 12-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||LT1 Chop Top||12-20-2001||05:44 PM||||I have the optima yellow top battery in my 88 GT.  I was told NOT to use the red top because it didn't stand up very well in the hot Fiero engine compartment. FWIW<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lt1choptopsig_1.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000007||chester||12-20-2001||07:28 PM||||I've tried both the yellow top and the red top in my GT and BOTH of them failed. I've had one in my Dodge Intrepid for over two years now with no problems. As a matter of fact I WAS impressed with the reserve time that the deep cycle had along with the quick recovery time.  The one in the Dodge is still going strong. In the Fiero the yellow top lasted me 7 months and the red top is only 5 months old and already showing the same problems.  I had a Sears Diehard Gold in it originally WITH NO PROBLEMS!  So, Back to the Sears Diehard I go.  Just my 2 cents.<P>Rob D.<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">       <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension||||reg||13
Z||000008||JD86GT350||12-20-2001||09:33 PM||||Any new battery I buy, I buy Optima.  I had one in my old Ranger, for 5 years I jumpstarted every college friend I had in -30 weather with no block heater.  I also ran a decent stereo system off it.  There was no heat issue in the Ranger though, then again there's no heat issue with my Optima in the Fiero either, since its in the front.||||reg||1
